# A FIXED DEFECT, named after it (Go's `test/fixedbugs`).
#
# SYMPTOM (2026-08-10, M5c step 6): `p.cells @ [7, 8]` printed the right answer and
# then `panic: 1 heap blocks still live at exit (a missing decref)`. Under
# `--sanitize`, ASan fired too.
#
# CAUSE: the ownership pass's rule 3 — a store increfs the new value before decrefing
# the old — asked whether the ROOT SLOT's type was counted. For a whole-slot store
# that is the same question as the stored value's type, so it had been right for two
# milestones. For a path store it is a different question: the slot is a `Row`, which
# is counted because it *contains* an array, while the place being written is the
# `[i64]` itself. The store was therefore treated as uncounted: the new array was
# never increfed and the old one never released.
#
# FIX: rule 3 reads the stored value's type. An *index* path is deliberately not
# covered — that one needs copy-on-write and the gate refuses it until the primitive
# exists.
#
# The leak counter is what found this. ASan agreed, but the counter named it in one
# line at exit; the shape of the bug is a missing decref, and a live-block balance is
# the instrument that sees exactly that.

record Row
    cells: [i64]

record Pair
    left: Row
    right: Row

function main()
    p: Row @ Row(cells: [9])
    print(p.cells[0], len(p.cells))

    # The write that leaked: a counted place reached through a field.
    p.cells @ [7, 8]
    print(p.cells[0], len(p.cells))

    # Twice over, so a leak would grow rather than sit still.
    p.cells @ [1]
    p.cells @ [2, 3, 4]
    print(len(p.cells))

    # Two levels deep, and through a record that holds two of them.
    q: Pair @ Pair(left: Row(cells: [1]), right: Row(cells: [2]))
    q.left @ Row(cells: [5, 6])
    print(q.left.cells[1], q.right.cells[0])

    # Assigning a field over itself: the incref must precede the decref.
    q.right @ q.right
    print(len(q.right.cells))
